<section class="legal-hero">
  <div class="legal-hero-badge">Legal & Privacy</div>
  <h1 class="legal-hero-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
  <div class="legal-hero-meta">Last updated: August 27th, 2026</div>
</section>

<section class="legal-body">
  <div class="legal-container">
    <main class="legal-card">
      <div class="legal-preamble">
        This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>Hope Vision AI Pvt. Ltd.</strong> (“Hope Vision AI”, “Lookify”, “we”, “us” or “our”) collects, uses, discloses, shares, stores and protects information in connection with the Lookify AI virtual try-on application (the “App”), whether accessed by (a) shoppers on a merchant's online store where the App is installed (“Customers”, “Shoppers”, “you”), (b) merchants who install and administer the App via the Shopify platform (“Merchants”), or (c) individuals who contact Lookify for support or otherwise interact directly with us. This Policy should be read together with our Terms & Conditions, Merchant Terms of Service, End User License Agreement, Cookie Policy and, where applicable, our Data Processing Addendum.
      </div>

      <section id="sec-1" class="legal-section">
        <h2 class="legal-section-title"><span class="legal-section-num">1</span> Definitions</h2>
        <p class="legal-text">For the purposes of this Policy:</p>
        <ul class="legal-list">
          <li class="legal-list-item"><strong>“Merchant”:</strong> A fashion house, brand or retailer that runs a Shopify store and uses the App to offer virtual try-on to its customers and shoppers.</li>
          <li class="legal-list-item"><strong>“Shopper(s)” or “Customer(s)”:</strong> A person who uses the try-on feature while shopping on a Merchant's store.</li>
          <li class="legal-list-item"><strong>“User Image”:</strong> The photo or selfie you upload to try a product on.</li>
          <li class="legal-list-item"><strong>“Result Image”:</strong> The AI-generated picture that shows the product on you, made from your photo and the product image.</li>
          <li class="legal-list-item"><strong>“Merchant Content”:</strong> The product images, product details and branding that a Merchant provides.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="sec-2" class="legal-section">
        <h2 class="legal-section-title"><span class="legal-section-num">2</span> Roles: Controller and Processor</h2>
        <p class="legal-text"><strong>2.1 Merchant Controller Role:</strong> When a Merchant installs the App on its Shopify store, the Merchant is generally the data controller/fiduciary in respect of its Shoppers' personal data, and Hope Vision AI acts as a data processor providing the try-on service on the Merchant's instructions.</p>
        <p class="legal-text"><strong>2.2 Hope Vision AI Fiduciary Role:</strong> Hope Vision AI additionally acts as a data controller/fiduciary in its own right in respect of: (a) Merchant account and billing information; (b) support communications; (c) security and fraud-prevention information; (d) service administration; (e) aggregated or de-identified product analytics; and (f) any information a Shopper elects to provide directly to Hope Vision AI (e.g., support requests).</p>
      </section>

      <section id="sec-3" class="legal-section">
        <h2 class="legal-section-title"><span class="legal-section-num">3</span> Information We Collect</h2>
        <ul class="legal-list">
          <li class="legal-list-item"><strong>Name:</strong> The name provided by the Customer/Shopper when using the App.</li>
          <li class="legal-list-item"><strong>Email address:</strong> The email address provided by the Customer/Shopper, used for account and communication purposes, including delivering try-on results.</li>
          <li class="legal-list-item"><strong>User Images:</strong> The photograph(s) or selfie(s) uploaded by the Shopper (“User Images”) for the virtual try-on feature.</li>
          <li class="legal-list-item"><strong>Result Images:</strong> The AI-generated virtual try-on image(s) (“Result Images”) produced using a User Image and product imagery.</li>
          <li class="legal-list-item"><strong>Products tried:</strong> Information about which products a Shopper has tried on using the App.</li>
          <li class="legal-list-item"><strong>Date and time:</strong> The date and time of each try-on session and related interaction with the App.</li>
          <li class="legal-list-item"><strong>Phone number and verification data:</strong> Where a Shopper chooses to receive a Result Image via WhatsApp, email or another supported channel, or where phone verification is required, we collect the phone number and related one-time-password (OTP) or verification records needed to deliver the requested result, verify the Shopper, and prevent misuse or fraud. A phone number collected for result delivery is not automatically used for marketing.</li>
          <li class="legal-list-item"><strong>Device and usage data:</strong> Technical information such as device type, browser, IP address (or a privacy-protected form of it), approximate location, session activity, try-on events, feature usage, and error/performance information.</li>
          <li class="legal-list-item"><strong>Merchant and store data:</strong> Store identifiers and domain, app installation information, Shopify access tokens, product catalogue and imagery, store branding and settings, billing status, and contact info via Shopify APIs.</li>
          <li class="legal-list-item"><strong>Support communications:</strong> Information contained in support requests, including contact details and technical logs.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="sec-4" class="legal-section">
        <h2 class="legal-section-title"><span class="legal-section-num">4</span> How We Use Information</h2>
        <p class="legal-text"><strong>4.1 User Image Usage:</strong> User Images are used solely to: (a) generate the requested virtual try-on visualization; (b) improve the accuracy and realism of our AI models, only where the Shopper has given explicit, opt-in consent for such use; and (c) provide customer support relating to the specific try-on session.</p>
        <p class="legal-text"><strong>4.2 Operational Usage:</strong> Device, usage, store, product and account data are used to: operate and maintain the App; authenticate users; deliver Result Images; provide WhatsApp or email sharing; maintain Merchant configurations; process billing; prevent fraud; diagnose issues; and fulfill legal obligations.</p>
        <div class="legal-callout">
          <p><strong>Anti-Commercialization Guarantee:</strong> We do not use User Images or Result Images for advertising or marketing purposes, and we never sell User Images or personal information to any third party.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="sec-5" class="legal-section">
        <h2 class="legal-section-title"><span class="legal-section-num">5</span> Legal Basis for Processing</h2>
        <p class="legal-text"><strong>5.1 Consent for Photos:</strong> We process User Images on the basis of the Customer's/Shopper's explicit, freely given consent, obtained at the point of upload through a clear affirmative action (e.g., a checkbox or “Upload & Try On” button following disclosure of this Policy).</p>
        <p class="legal-text"><strong>5.2 Statutory Grounds:</strong> We process other categories of data on the basis of: performance of contract, legitimate interests in operating and securing the App, and compliance with legal obligations under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (“DPDP Act”) and, where applicable, EU/UK GDPR.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="sec-6" class="legal-section">
        <h2 class="legal-section-title"><span class="legal-section-num">6</span> AI Model Training, Product Improvement and Consent</h2>
        <p class="legal-text">User Images are not used for AI-model training by default. If Lookify offers a separate program allowing Shoppers to contribute images toward AI or model improvement, participation will require a separate, explicit and optional opt-in consent. Declining such consent will not prevent the Shopper from using the standard virtual try-on service. A Shopper who has opted in may subsequently withdraw that consent and request deletion at any time.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="sec-7" class="legal-section">
        <h2 class="legal-section-title"><span class="legal-section-num">7</span> Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
        <p class="legal-text">We follow a data-minimization approach and retain personal information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purpose for which it was collected:</p>
        <ul class="legal-list">
          <li class="legal-list-item"><strong>User Images:</strong> By default, User Images are processed transiently to generate the try-on result and are automatically deleted from active processing systems within 24 hours of the session, and are not retained thereafter, unless separately opted in under Clause 6.</li>
          <li class="legal-list-item"><strong>Result Images:</strong> Temporarily stored to allow viewing, downloading or sharing. Automatically deleted when the account becomes inactive/deleted unless explicitly saved by the user.</li>
          <li class="legal-list-item"><strong>Saved Profile Photos:</strong> Retained until deleted or replaced by the Shopper, or upon account deletion.</li>
          <li class="legal-list-item"><strong>Phone Numbers & Verification Data:</strong> Retained for authentication and security; operational retention period is 1 year.</li>
          <li class="legal-list-item"><strong>Merchant Data:</strong> Retained while active. Deleted or de-identified upon uninstallation or valid Shopify deletion request.</li>
          <li class="legal-list-item"><strong>Billing & Transaction Records:</strong> Retained as required for accounting, taxation, and statutory obligations.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="sec-8" class="legal-section">
        <h2 class="legal-section-title"><span class="legal-section-num">8</span> How Long We Keep Your Photo – In Plain Language</h2>
        <div class="legal-callout">
          <p>By default, your photo is used only to generate your try-on result and is automatically deleted from our systems within 24 hours – we do not keep it after that unless you've opted in under Clause 6.</p>
        </div>
        <p class="legal-text">We keep images for this short 24-hour window (rather than deleting them the instant a result is generated) to: (a) let you view, re-download or share your result; (b) understand overall usage patterns and service reliability; (c) troubleshoot session issues; and (d) allow optional comparison where requested.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="sec-9" class="legal-section">
        <h2 class="legal-section-title"><span class="legal-section-num">9</span> Collecting and Managing Your Pictures</h2>
        <p class="legal-text"><strong>9.1 Collection:</strong> We collect a picture only when you actively choose to upload or capture one for virtual try-on.</p>
        <p class="legal-text"><strong>9.2 Processing & Access:</strong> Once uploaded, pictures are processed by our AI systems. Photos are never viewed by staff except when necessary to investigate a specific technical support request.</p>
        <p class="legal-text"><strong>9.3 Deletion:</strong> Pictures are deleted automatically at the end of the retention window using non-recoverable erasure processes.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="sec-10" class="legal-section">
        <h2 class="legal-section-title"><span class="legal-section-num">10</span> Shopify Privacy Requests</h2>
        <p class="legal-text">We support applicable privacy requests received through Shopify, including requests relating to: access to stored customer data; deletion/redaction of customer data; and deletion/redaction of store information following uninstall.</p>
      </section>

